{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/electrolysis-basics/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/electrolysis-basics.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Electrolysis Basics | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Electrochemistry &amp; Redox\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-400 to-pink-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -bolt text-yellow-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"bolt\">bolt</span>Electrolysis Basics\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding the principles of electrolysis, electrolytic cells, and industrial applications.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-rose-50 border-l-4 border-rose-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define electrolysis and identify its key components</li>\n          <li>• Distinguish between electrolytic and electrochemical cells</li>\n          <li>• Predict products at the anode and cathode</li>\n          <li>• Explain industrial applications of electrolysis</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is Electrolysis? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is Electrolysis?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-rose-600\">Electrolysis</strong> is the process of using electrical energy to drive a non-spontaneous chemical reaction. It involves passing an electric current through an electrolyte (molten or aqueous ionic compound) to decompose it into its elements.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mt-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Key Components:</p>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li><strong>Electrolyte:</strong> An ionic compound (molten or in solution) that conducts electricity</li>\n              <li><strong>Anode (+):</strong> Positive electrode where oxidation occurs</li>\n              <li><strong>Cathode (-):</strong> Negative electrode where reduction occurs</li>\n              <li><strong>Power source:</strong> Battery or DC power supply that provides electrical energy</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Diagram -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center\">\n            <svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 250\" class=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\">\n              <!-- Battery -->\n              <rect x=\"170\" y=\"10\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#4a5568\" rx=\"3\"></rect>\n              <rect x=\"190\" y=\"5\" width=\"20\" height=\"5\" fill=\"#4a5568\"></rect>\n              <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"12\">Battery</text>\n              <text x=\"200\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a5568\" font-size=\"10\">DC Power</text>\n              \n              <!-- Wires -->\n              <line x1=\"190\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#e53e3e\" stroke-width=\"3\"></line>\n              <line x1=\"210\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#3182ce\" stroke-width=\"3\"></line>\n              \n              <!-- Electrodes -->\n              <rect x=\"85\" y=\"80\" width=\"30\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#718096\" rx=\"2\"></rect>\n              <rect x=\"285\" y=\"80\" width=\"30\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#718096\" rx=\"2\"></rect>\n              \n              <!-- Labels for electrodes -->\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e53e3e\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cathode (-)</text>\n              <text x=\"300\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3182ce\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Anode (+)</text>\n              \n              <!-- Electrolyte container -->\n              <rect x=\"60\" y=\"80\" width=\"280\" height=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a5568\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"5\"></rect>\n              <rect x=\"62\" y=\"82\" width=\"276\" height=\"96\" fill=\"#bee3f8\" opacity=\"0.5\"></rect>\n              \n              <!-- Ions in solution -->\n              <circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"120\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e53e3e\"></circle>\n              <text x=\"130\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"10\">+</text>\n              <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"150\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e53e3e\"></circle>\n              <text x=\"170\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"10\">+</text>\n              <circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"110\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#3182ce\"></circle>\n              <text x=\"250\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"10\">-</text>\n              <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"145\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#3182ce\"></circle>\n              <text x=\"230\" y=\"149\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"10\">-</text>\n              \n              <!-- Labels -->\n              <text x=\"200\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a5568\" font-size=\"12\">Electrolyte (ions in solution)</text>\n              <text x=\"130\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e53e3e\" font-size=\"10\">Cations</text>\n              <text x=\"260\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3182ce\" font-size=\"10\">Anions</text>\n            </svg>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-center text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Schematic diagram of an electrolytic cell</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: What Happens at the Electrodes? -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          What Happens at the Electrodes?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -minus-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>At the Cathode (-)\n            </h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• <strong>Reduction</strong> occurs (gain of electrons)</li>\n              <li>• Cations migrate here</li>\n              <li>• Cations gain electrons and become neutral</li>\n              <li>• For molten electrolytes: Metal forms</li>\n              <li>• For aqueous solutions: Check electrochemical series</li>\n            </ul>\n            <div class=\"mt-3 bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n              <code class=\"text-red-600\">M<sup>n+</sup> + ne<sup>-</sup> → M</code>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -plus-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"add_circle\">add_circle</span>At the Anode (+)\n            </h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• <strong>Oxidation</strong> occurs (loss of electrons)</li>\n              <li>• Anions migrate here</li>\n              <li>• Anions lose electrons and become neutral</li>\n              <li>• For molten electrolytes: Non-metal forms</li>\n              <li>• For aqueous: Check discharge preference</li>\n            </ul>\n            <div class=\"mt-3 bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n              <code class=\"text-blue-600\">A<sup>n-</sup> → A + ne<sup>-</sup></code>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 1 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-rose-50 text-left font-semibold text-rose-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-rose-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example: Electrolysis of Molten NaCl</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Predict the products when molten sodium chloride is electrolyzed.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-rose-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Identify the ions present</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-rose-700 font-mono mt-1\">Na<sup>+</sup> (cations) and Cl<sup>-</sup> (anions)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-red-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> At the cathode (reduction)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-red-700 font-mono mt-1\">Na<sup>+</sup> + e<sup>-</sup> → Na (sodium metal)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> At the anode (oxidation)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">2Cl<sup>-</sup> → Cl<sub>2</sub> + 2e<sup>-</sup> (chlorine gas)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Products:</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700\">Cathode: Sodium metal (Na)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700\">Anode: Chlorine gas (Cl₂)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Electrolysis of Aqueous Solutions -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Electrolysis of Aqueous Solutions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Important:</strong> In aqueous solutions, water molecules dissociate into H<sup>+</sup> and OH<sup>-</sup> ions, which compete with the electrolyte ions for discharge.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Discharge Preferences (Selective Discharge)</h3>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <p class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\">At the Cathode:</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2\">The ion lower in the electrochemical series is discharged preferentially.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">If metal is above Zn: H₂ is produced instead</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">If metal is below Zn: Metal is deposited</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <p class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\">At the Anode:</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2\">Order of discharge preference:</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">1. Halides (Cl⁻, Br⁻, I⁻)</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">2. OH⁻ → O₂</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">3. Other anions (not discharged)</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 2 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example: Electrolysis of Dilute NaCl(aq)</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Predict the products when dilute sodium chloride solution is electrolyzed.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Ions present:</strong> Na<sup>+</sup>, H<sup>+</sup> (cations); Cl<sup>-</sup>, OH<sup>-</sup> (anions)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-red-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>At Cathode:</strong> H<sup>+</sup> is discharged (Na is more reactive than H)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-red-700 font-mono mt-1\">2H<sup>+</sup> + 2e<sup>-</sup> → H<sub>2</sub> (hydrogen gas)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>At Anode:</strong> OH<sup>-</sup> is discharged (Cl⁻ concentration is low)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">4OH<sup>-</sup> → 2H<sub>2</sub>O + O<sub>2</sub> + 4e<sup>-</sup></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-purple-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Products:</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700\">Cathode: Hydrogen gas (H₂)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700\">Anode: Oxygen gas (O₂)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm mt-1\">NaOH remains in solution (alkaline)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Industrial Applications -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Industrial Applications\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mb-2\">\n              <span class=\"mi -industry text-gray-600 mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Extraction of Metals</h4>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Aluminium, sodium, and magnesium are extracted by electrolysis of their molten ores.</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mb-2\">\n              <span class=\"mi -coins text-yellow-600 mr-2\" data-mi=\"paid\">paid</span>\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Electroplating</h4>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Coating objects with a thin layer of metal (e.g., silver plating, gold plating) for protection or decoration.</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mb-2\">\n              <span class=\"mi -tint text-blue-600 mr-2\" data-mi=\"water_drop\">water_drop</span>\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Purification of Copper</h4>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Impure copper is made the anode; pure copper deposits at the cathode. Impurities fall as anode sludge.</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mb-2\">\n              <span class=\"mi -flask text-green-600 mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Manufacturing</h4>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Production of chlorine, hydrogen, and sodium hydroxide from brine (chlor-alkali process).</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-blue-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. What are the products of electrolyzing molten lead(II) bromide, PbBr₂?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cathode: Pb²⁺ + 2e⁻ → <strong>Pb</strong> (lead metal)</p>\n                <p>Anode: 2Br⁻ → Br₂ + 2e⁻ → <strong>Br₂</strong> (bromine gas)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Predict the products when concentrated NaCl(aq) is electrolyzed.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cathode: 2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → <strong>H₂</strong> (hydrogen)</p>\n                <p>Anode: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻ → <strong>Cl₂</strong> (chlorine)</p>\n                <p>Note: At high Cl⁻ concentration, chloride is discharged at anode.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Why is cryolite used in the extraction of aluminium?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) is used to:</p>\n                <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                  <li>Lower the melting point of Al₂O₃ (from 2050°C to about 950°C)</li>\n                  <li>Reduce energy costs</li>\n                  <li>Improve conductivity of the electrolyte</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-rose-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• Electrolysis uses electrical energy to decompose compounds</li>\n            <li>• Reduction occurs at cathode (gain electrons); Oxidation at anode (lose electrons)</li>\n            <li>• In aqueous solutions, H⁺ and OH⁻ compete with electrolyte ions</li>\n            <li>• The electrochemical series helps predict discharge products</li>\n            <li>• Applications include metal extraction, electroplating, and chemical manufacturing</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-50 to-pink-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card {\n      transition: all 0.2s ease;\n    }\n    .step-card:hover {\n      transform: translateX(4px);\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn {\n      transition: all 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover {\n      transform: scale(1.02);\n    }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"electrolysis-basics","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What is electrolysis?","options":["Using chemical energy to produce electricity","Using electrical energy to drive a non-spontaneous reaction","A spontaneous redox reaction","The flow of electrons through a wire"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Electrolysis uses electrical energy from an external source to drive a non-spontaneous chemical reaction."},{"question":"At which electrode does oxidation occur during electrolysis?","options":["Cathode","Anode","Both electrodes","Neither electrode"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Oxidation (loss of electrons) always occurs at the anode, which is the positive electrode in electrolysis."},{"question":"What happens at the cathode during electrolysis?","options":["Oxidation","Electrons are lost","Reduction","Anions are attracted"],"correct":2,"explanation":"At the cathode (negative electrode), reduction occurs as cations gain electrons."},{"question":"In the electrolysis of molten NaCl, what product forms at the cathode?","options":["Chlorine gas","Sodium metal","Hydrogen gas","Oxygen gas"],"correct":1,"explanation":"At the cathode: Na⁺ + e⁻ → Na. Sodium ions are reduced to sodium metal."},{"question":"Why might H₂ be produced instead of a metal at the cathode during electrolysis of aqueous solutions?","options":["The metal is less reactive than hydrogen","Hydrogen is always produced in aqueous solutions","The metal is more reactive than hydrogen","Water is a better conductor"],"correct":2,"explanation":"If the metal is more reactive (higher in the electrochemical series) than hydrogen, H⁺ from water is discharged instead, producing H₂."},{"question":"What determines which ion is discharged preferentially at the anode?","options":["The size of the ion","The color of the ion","Position in the electrochemical series","The temperature of the solution"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The electrochemical series determines discharge preference. Halides are discharged before OH⁻, which is discharged before other anions."},{"question":"In the chlor-alkali process, what products are obtained from concentrated NaCl solution?","options":["Na, Cl₂, H₂O","H₂, Cl₂, NaOH","O₂, H₂, NaCl","Na, O₂, HCl"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Electrolysis of concentrated brine produces H₂ at cathode, Cl₂ at anode, and NaOH remains in solution."},{"question":"What is the purpose of cryolite in aluminium extraction?","options":["To increase the melting point of Al₂O₃","To produce chlorine gas","To lower the melting point and save energy","To prevent oxidation of aluminium"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) lowers the melting point of Al₂O₃ from 2050°C to about 950°C, reducing energy costs."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"electrolysis-basics","topicTitle":"Electrolysis Basics","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}